# Backup output never belongs in this public repo — it carries recent-activity
# history (recent folders, Go-to-Folder history) that leaks client names and
# directory layouts. bkp writes to $BKP_ROOT (~/Documents/bkp) instead; this
# entry only catches output from an older copy of the script.
macos/snapshot/

# Same reasoning for the other bkp targets, whose output is worse: Claude
# transcripts carry client code and anything ever pasted into a prompt.
#
# bkp itself now lives in the private-dotfiles repo, and its real defence is
# bkp_assert_not_in_git, which refuses to write anywhere inside a work tree.
# These entries are the second line, kept here because THIS is the repo a
# stray snapshot would be published from: they name every category bkp can
# create at any depth — a category missing here is one this file fails to
# catch.
macos-defaults/
sublime-session/
claude-context/
*.tar.gz
